WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:07.956
A rental listing can promise running water without showing the tank.
ScoutVault lets you ask someone nearby to check the place before you send
a deposit.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:22.644
This sample studio in Akoka lists an address, a yearly price, and a water
tank. I’m using test tokens on Solana devnet.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:34.060
I paste the listing link. Firecrawl reads the page, and ScoutVault turns
those three details into questions. I can edit each question and move the
entrance pin.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:53.244
I set the reward at two test tokens. The Solana program holds them for
this check, so the scout can see the reward is funded before accepting.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:12.764
I switch to the scout wallet and claim the check. Only one scout can
claim it. The scout can read the questions or have the device read them
aloud.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:32.860
The scout answers each question and attaches a photo. Here I’m using a
labelled illustration. The water tank stays marked as unconfirmed.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:56.820
The scout signs the report. ScoutVault checks the photo and signature
against what was submitted. The requester sees the answers and approves
this exact report.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:20.212
The scout’s balance increases by two tokens. Solana Explorer shows the
devnet payout and its confirmed transaction.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.612
The requester now has the signed report and the payout receipt.
